ments at 3162 and 3189 and the typed error text (\\\"reject this approval\\\", line 3147) are also stale for this case.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":221,\"summary\":\"R1 gaps: a heading \\\"### Accepted --> limits\\\" (stray close marker) or a comment opened in the heading words and closed on the next line yields no limits and no problem.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":122,\"summary\":\"R3 gap: indent counts characters, so a tab-indented (or two spaces plus tab) code block of backticks still opens a fence that silently hides a later accepted limits section.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":125,\"summary\":\"R3 side effect: a fence nested in a list item at four spaces is no longer a fence, so a comment opener shown inside it now refuses every limit as unterminated, where the base engine sealed them. It fails closed and visibly, but no decision records the changed answer.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N7\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\".pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-review-declared-limits-residuals.md\",\"line\":81,\"summary\":\"The stated technical risk is false: a code span continued over two lines whose second line holds a comment opener, closed by a later comment closer, hides the accepted limits section with no limit and no problem. The base engine behaves the same.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N8\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":301,\"summary\":\"Stale doc comments: htmlCommentStart still describes the odd-backtick-count rule that R2 replaced, and line 256 refers to the removed acceptedLimitsOf.\"}' '],' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\